    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d717">

                <pb facs="0836" n="1670" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1670"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 652.119/605</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-05T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 5, 1918, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6772. Following telegram, dated March 2, has been received by the Department from
                    the American Ambassador at Madrid: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>French Embassy requests Department be informed that matter of Spanish
                            exterior <hi rendition="#italic">rentes</hi> in which Spanish Government
                            is much interested, is being withheld from French-Spanish agreement and
                            for future consideration in connection with English credit. Embassy
                            approved of this course and is strongly of opinion that French-Spanish
                            agreement will be irretrievably lost if question of English credit is
                            injected therein. Embassy stands ready to ratify Spanish-American
                            agreement as modified by Department’s 914, February 26, 8 p.m.<anchor
                                n="1" xml:id="d717-f1"/> English are apparently desirous to delay
                            ratification and to reopen negotiations.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Department has been advised by the French representatives here that the
                    French-Spanish agreement has been ready for signature by the Spanish Prime
                    Minister since February 28.</p>
                <p>Department wishes you to make representations to the British Government to the
                    effect that this Government considers it highly desirable that ratification of
                    the French-Spanish and Spanish-American agreements be no longer delayed. Please
                    report at once by cable result of your representations.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
